# EXAMPLE crew script: bring up four GPCs and two CRTs through the NBAT to
# OPS 2, waiting on the O6 MODE talkbacks rather than fixed times.  One file
# holds the switches and the keystrokes; panelO6.py plays it (crewscript.py).
# Run from discretePanel/:
#
#   python3 simulatePASS.py --gpcs 1-4 --crts 2 --tape OI340700-v44boot.mmv \
#       --script examples/4gpc-startup.script --duration 900
#
# Every time is written +N: N seconds after the line before (or after the
# wait above it), so a line can be inserted without renumbering the rest.  The
# one delay that is still a fixed time is STBY to ITEM 1 EXEC (67 s for GPC1,
# 65 s for the others), for the IPL display to come up.
#
# Verified 2026-09-15: four GPCs to OPS 2, with no CAM lamp.  As two files, OPS
# 2 was typed about 570 s after the panel started, against 840 s with fixed
# times.  This +N spelling resolves to exactly the times of the verified file.

wait user
3  subtitle First, power on each GPC. (Look in the upper left of the panel.)
+2 gpc 1
+0 power on
+1 gpc 2
+0 power on
+1 gpc 3
+0 power on
+1 gpc 4
+0 power on

# --- all four GPCs to HALT, the IDPs on, GPC1 IPL from MM1 on CRT 1 ---------
+1 subtitle Put each GPC into HALT mode.\nThat's the default, so you may see nothing happen.\nLook in the lower left of the panel.
+2 gpc 1
+0 mode HALT
+0 gpc 2
+1 mode HALT
+0 gpc 3
+1 mode HALT
+0 gpc 4
+1 mode HALT

+1 subtitle Power up IDP 1 and 2. Look in the upper right of the panel.
+2 idppower 1 on
+1 idppower 2 on

+1 subtitle Select CRT "1+2" (CRT1). Look at the very top of the panel.
+2 crt 1

+1 subtitle Select IPL source MM1. Look in more-or-less in the middle of the panel.
+2 source MM1

+1 subtitle Press IPL button for GPC 1 to load the bootstrap program\nKeep your eye on the ACTIVITY MM1 / MM2 indicators just above.
+2 gpc 1
+0 ipl

+1 subtitle Flip the spring-loaded toggle for IDP 1 LOAD.\nLook midway up the right-hand side.
+2 idpload 1

+1 subtitle Switch GPC1 from HALT mode to STBY mode
+2 mode STANDBY

+1 subtitle And now we wait for the 2nd-stage bootloader to run ...
wait crt 1 title GPCIPL MENU
+0 subtitle It's up! Observe the title "GPCIPL MENU (1) ... 1".

+5 subtitle Let's command a load of OPS 0 in GPC 1\nby pressing keys on the left keyboard
+5 subtitle <left>Use the keys ITEM 1 EXEC
+2 keys ITEM
+1 keys 1
+1 keys EXEC
+2 subtitle Wait for it to load and run ...
wait gpc 1 mode-tb RUN timeout 300
+2 subtitle Switch BFC CRT DISPLAY OFF
+1 crt 0
+2 subtitle Change GPC 1 mode from STBY to RUN
+2 mode RUN
wait crt 1 title "GPC MEMORY" 
+0 subtitle It's up! Notice the title "GPC MEMORY"
+3 subtitle And turn OFF the IPL source
+2 source OFF

# --- GPC1 loaded: to RUN; GPC2 IPL on CRT 2 ----------------------------------
+2 subtitle Now repeat that whole exercise for GPC 2.
+0 gpc 2
+3 subtitle Select CRT "2+3" (CRT2).
# Deassign CRT 2 from PASS before lending it to the GPC being IPLed,
# "to avoid any conflict in CRT commanders" (DPS Workbook USA005350
# Rev B).  Keyed on KB1 because GPC/CRT entries go to a
# PASS-commanded CRT.
+2 keys KB1 GPC/CRT 0 2 EXEC
+2 crt 2

+1 subtitle Select IPL source MM1
+2 source MM1

+1 subtitle Press IPL button for GPC 2 to load the bootstrap program.
+2 ipl

+1 subtitle Flip the spring-loaded toggle for IDP 2 LOAD.
+2 idpload 2

+1 subtitle Switch GPC 1 from HALT mode to STBY mode
+2 mode STANDBY

+1 subtitle And now we wait for the 2nd-stage bootloader to run ...
wait crt 2 title GPCIPL MENU
+0 subtitle It's up! Observe the title "GPCIPL MENU (1) ... 2".

+5 subtitle Let's command a load of OPS 0 in GPC 2\nby pressing keys on the right keyboard
+5 subtitle <right>Use the keys ITEM 1 EXEC
+2 keys KB2 ITEM
+1 keys KB2 1
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+2 subtitle Wait for it to load and run ...
wait gpc 2 mode-tb RUN timeout 300
+2 subtitle Switch BFC CRT DISPLAY OFF
+1 crt 0
+2 subtitle Change GPC 2 mode from STBY to RUN
+2 mode RUN
# Give GPC 2 the display now that it is in RUN -- "It is assigned an
# IDP to ensure that it is running properly" -- before looking for its
# GPC MEMORY page, which only appears once a GPC commands the CRT.
+2 keys KB1 GPC/CRT 2 2 EXEC
wait crt 2 title "GPC MEMORY" 
+0 subtitle It's up! Notice the title "GPC MEMORY"
+3 subtitle And turn OFF the IPL source
+2 source OFF

# --- GPC2 loaded: to RUN; GPC3 IPL -------------------------------------------
+2 subtitle Now repeat that whole exercise for GPC 3.
+3 subtitle CRT "2+3" should already still be selected
# Deassign CRT 2 from PASS before lending it to the GPC being IPLed,
# "to avoid any conflict in CRT commanders" (DPS Workbook USA005350
# Rev B).  Keyed on KB1 because GPC/CRT entries go to a
# PASS-commanded CRT.
+2 keys KB1 GPC/CRT 0 2 EXEC
+1 crt 2

+1 subtitle Select IPL source MM1
+2 source MM1

+1 subtitle Press IPL button for GPC 3 to load the bootstrap program.
+2 gpc 3
+0 ipl

+1 subtitle Flip the spring-loaded toggle for IDP 2 LOAD.
+2 idpload 2

+1 subtitle Switch GPC 3 from HALT mode to STBY mode
+2 mode STANDBY

+1 subtitle And now we wait for the 2nd-stage bootloader to run ...
wait crt 2 title GPCIPL MENU
+0 subtitle It's up! Observe the title "GPCIPL MENU (1) ... 3".

+5 subtitle Let's command a load of OPS 0 in GPC 3\nby pressing keys on the right keyboard
+5 subtitle <right>Use the keys ITEM 1 EXEC
+2 keys KB2 ITEM
+1 keys KB2 1
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+2 subtitle Wait for it to load and run ...
wait gpc 3 mode-tb RUN timeout 300
+2 subtitle Switch BFC CRT DISPLAY OFF
+1 crt 0
+2 subtitle Change GPC 3 mode from STBY to RUN
+2 mode RUN
# Give GPC 3 the display now that it is in RUN -- "It is assigned an
# IDP to ensure that it is running properly" -- before looking for its
# GPC MEMORY page, which only appears once a GPC commands the CRT.
+2 keys KB1 GPC/CRT 3 2 EXEC
wait crt 2 title "GPC MEMORY"
+0 subtitle It's up! Notice the title "GPC MEMORY"
+3 subtitle And turn OFF the IPL source
+2 source OFF

# --- GPC3 loaded: to RUN; GPC4 IPL -------------------------------------------
+2 subtitle And GPC 4 should be almost the same thing as GPC 3.
+3 subtitle CRT "2+3" should already still be selected
# Deassign CRT 2 from PASS before lending it to the GPC being IPLed,
# "to avoid any conflict in CRT commanders" (DPS Workbook USA005350
# Rev B).  Keyed on KB1 because GPC/CRT entries go to a
# PASS-commanded CRT.
+2 keys KB1 GPC/CRT 0 2 EXEC
+1 crt 2

+1 subtitle Select IPL source MM1
+2 source MM1

+1 subtitle Press IPL button for GPC 4 to load the bootstrap program.
+2 gpc 4
+0 ipl

+1 subtitle Flip the spring-loaded toggle for IDP 2 LOAD.
+2 idpload 2

+1 subtitle Switch GPC 4 from HALT mode to STBY mode
+2 mode STANDBY

+1 subtitle And now we wait for the 2nd-stage bootloader to run ...
wait crt 2 title GPCIPL MENU
+0 subtitle It's up! Observe the title "GPCIPL MENU (1) ... 4".

+5 subtitle Let's command a load of OPS 0 in GPC 4\nby pressing keys on the right keyboard
+5 subtitle <right>Use the keys ITEM 1 EXEC
+2 keys KB2 ITEM
+1 keys KB2 1
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+2 subtitle Wait for it to load and run ...
wait gpc 4 mode-tb RUN timeout 300
+2 subtitle Switch BFC CRT DISPLAY OFF
+1 crt 0
+2 subtitle Change GPC 4 mode from STBY to RUN
+2 mode RUN
# Give GPC 4 the display now that it is in RUN -- "It is assigned an
# IDP to ensure that it is running properly" -- before looking for its
# GPC MEMORY page, which only appears once a GPC commands the CRT.
+2 keys KB1 GPC/CRT 4 2 EXEC
wait crt 2 title "GPC MEMORY" 
+0 subtitle It's up! Notice the title "GPC MEMORY"
+3 subtitle And turn OFF the IPL source
+2 source OFF

# Assign GPC 2 its display, now that every GPC has been IPLed.  The real
# procedure assigns each GPC an IDP once it is moded to RUN ("It is
# assigned an IDP to ensure that it is running properly", DPS Workbook
# USA005350 Rev B).  It goes AFTER the last IPL because each IPL in turn
# borrows CRT 2 through the BFC CRT switches, which would undo it.
# Without this CRT 2 stays with GPC 1, and both computers command that
# bus -- which the Workbook says to avoid (ledger #184).
+2 subtitle Assign CRT 2 to GPC 2, so GPC 2 drives its own display.
+2 keys KB1 GPC/CRT 2 2 EXEC
wait crt 2 title "GPC MEMORY" timeout 60

# --- GPC4 loaded: to RUN; the NBAT, then OPS 2 -------------------------------
+1 subtitle Now we have to configure the databuses.
+3 subtitle Let's use the right keyboard, just for fun, but either works.
+3 subtitle <right>ITEM 1 + 2 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM
+1 keys KB2 1
+1 keys KB2 +
+1 keys KB2 2
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 2 + 1 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 2 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 3 + 2 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 3 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 2 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 4 + 3 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 4 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 3 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 5 + 4 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 5 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 4 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 7 + 1 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 7 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 8 + 2 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 8 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 2 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 9 + 3 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 9 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 3 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 1 0 + 4 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 0 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 4 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 1 1 + 1 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 1 2 + 1 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 2 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 1 3 + 1 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 3 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 2 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 1 8 + 1 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 8 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC
+1 subtitle <right>ITEM 1 9 + 1 EXEC
+1 keys KB2 ITEM 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 9 
+1 keys KB2 + 
+1 keys KB2 2 
+1 keys KB2 EXEC

+2 subtitle Finally, let's transition from OPS 0 to OPS 2\nAll 4 GPCs will do this at once.\nEither keyboard can be used.
+3 subtitle <right>OPS 2 0 1 PRO
+1 keys KB2 OPS 
+1 keys KB2 2 
+1 keys KB2 0 
+1 keys KB2 1 
+1 keys KB2 PRO
+1 subtitle And wait for it to load ...
wait crt 2 title "UNIV PTG"
+0 subtitle It looks like it worked, since we're at the "UNIV PTG" screen!\nNotice the "2011" in the upper right corner as well.
+5 subtitle Hopefully there are no indicators lit on the CAM\nThat means that the redundant GPCs are in sync!\nIf there are any lamps lit, one of them is out of favor.
+5 subtitle I'm all done here, but you can keep playing if you like ...
+5 subtitle
